== caller_misuse: three minimal callers, runnable transcripts ==
[FAKTA] FIPS 203 section 6.3: decapsulation uses no randomness and never signals failure; the accept/reject flag must not be returned in any form
setup: ML-KEM-768, genuine decaps == shared: True
-- scenario (i): no key confirmation, Kbar used as session key --
  tampered ct decaps -> session key: bc655b3027d548fe...
  same tampered ct decaps again -> identical key: True
  peer's true session key:          a0e28fccceab9b5f...
  caller key == peer key: False
  [ANALISIS] LEAK/BREAK: the caller silently uses Kbar as if it were K -- the session is broken (peer cannot decrypt anything), and the failure is deterministic: the same ciphertext always yields the same Kbar, so the rejection is replayable and recognisable across sessions
PASS MISUSE-NO-KCF -- Kbar used as session key, != peer K, deterministic across runs
-- scenario (ii): caller logs decapsulation outcomes --
  LOG: decaps ct=1d13cd98600a... REJECT
  LOG: decaps ct=1c13cd98600a... REJECT
  LOG: decaps ct=1c13cd98600a... REJECT
  LOG: decaps ct=1c13cd98600a... REJECT
  LOG: decaps ct=1c13cd98600a... ACCEPT
  [ANALISIS] LEAK/BREAK: the log records accept/reject for every chosen ciphertext -- a decryption-failure oracle written to disk. Anyone who can read the logs (or count log volume / error counters) learns exactly which crafted ciphertexts the key accepted, which is the oracle FIPS 203 section 6.3 forbids returning 'in any form'
PASS MISUSE-LOGS -- log lines leak ACCEPT/REJECT per chosen ciphertext
-- scenario (iii): caller retries a rejected ciphertext --
  retry 1 -> 84394f4492bfb2b7...
  retry 2 -> 84394f4492bfb2b7... (same: True)
  retry 3 -> 84394f4492bfb2b7... (same: True)
  fresh encapsulation decaps == shared: True
  [ANALISIS] LEAK/BREAK: retrying a rejected ciphertext never changes the outcome -- decapsulation is deterministic, so a retry loop burns queries and, against a static key, hands a key-mismatch attacker free oracle queries; only a fresh encapsulation can succeed
PASS MISUSE-RETRY -- 3 retries return identical Kbar; fresh encaps succeeds

CALLER_MISUSE VERDICT: PASS -- all three misuse transcripts demonstrate the concrete leak/break as specified
